Description: With the browser's own compositor in software, the page's two views are still declared to the desktop (ORDER 616)
 Under software WebRender (a machine or virtual machine without usable 3D, a blocklisted driver, gfx.webrender.software) the
 native Wayland compositor still gives a WebGL canvas a surface of its own (RenderCompositorNativeSWGL, shared memory buffers),
 but WebGL swaps through SurfaceFactory_Basic there (TexTypeForWebgl answers Unknown under software WebRender), and
 SetStereoMode wrote the mark only into a DMABuf. The pair was read back into an RGB buffer without a mark, WebRender gave the
 compositor surface no stereo mark, and Stereo KWin showed both views squeezed into the canvas's place, the same in each eye
 (+stereo3d14 in the rig: 604 commits of a 1600x450 shared memory buffer on the canvas's own subsurface, no kde_stereo_content).
 The mark now travels with the buffer read back (SetStereoMode returns it, PushRemoteTexture hands it to the remote texture's
 BufferTextureHost, whose RGB image descriptor carries it), so WebRender passes it to the compositor surface it draws the
 picture into, as it already did for video, and that surface is declared full side by side. One picture keeps mark 0: 2D
 canvases and the hardware route reach the compositor as before.
 With the mark, a canvas WebRender does not give a surface of its own (a rounded clip) is drawn into the page's tiles once
 per eye, as on the GPU route; under software WebRender the right eye then showed only the canvas's background, because
 brush_image's bounds for a rectangle texture started at the texture's origin instead of the eye's part (min_uv). They now
 start at min_uv for both kinds of texture; a whole image (min_uv 0) is drawn as before.
 Upstream: the stereo mark, the camera hack and the flat WebXR display are the edition's own (fork Sparky-OS/waterfox);
 Mozilla's software path on Wayland is RenderCompositorNativeSWGL (bug 1711224), unchanged here. Mozilla's current tree no
 longer has brush_image.glsl (images moved to the quad shaders), and no Bugzilla bug names this bound.
